European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen is delivering a major state of the European Union speech on Wednesday setting out her priorities for the next year and her vision for tackling the challenges faced by the world’s biggest trading bloc. France 24's Armen Georgian tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ebf218e-b1bc-11f1-93e9-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-120111-120802-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ebf218e-b1bc-11f1-93e9-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-120111-120802-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">453cd9de-b1bc-11f1-97a4-7fcbc7ea3ec8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:09:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>How is Democracy Doing?</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260916-how-is-democracy-doing</link><description>
For the UN's International Day of Democracy we ask: “how is democracy doing in France and globally?” We also take a look at Le Monde's Ipsos poll on the presidential election as well as studies on the effect US politics is having on democracy globally. Finally, we will break down a common misperception that backsliding is due to “democracy not delivering”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20b3d22c-b19c-11f1-9619-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8003198156aaa3e4243e5b1-17947063.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20b3d22c-b19c-11f1-9619-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8003198156aaa3e4243e5b1-17947063.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">509fa464-b19e-11f1-a3d8-a7aedb62b025</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:01:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Solange MOUGIN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Former Kosovo president sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-former-kosovo-president-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes</link><description>
Former Kosovo President Hashim Thaci was found guilty of war crimes committed as part of the Kosovo Liberation Army including murder, torture and illegal arrests by a tribunal in The Hague on Wednesday. Thaci was sentenced to 25 ​years in prison alongside fellow former KLA figures who were also found guilty and sentenced.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb01620-b1c9-11f1-8b3a-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CK27L.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb01620-b1c9-11f1-8b3a-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CK27L.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">977d0508-b1ca-11f1-aed3-cdcd2ee68797</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:55:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb01620-b1c9-11f1-8b3a-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CK27L.jpg">© Koen Van Weel, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>At least 60 killed in gold mine collapse in remote area of Sudan</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260916-sudan-gold-mine-collapse-kills-at-least-67-people</link><description>
A gold mine collapse on Wednesday killed at least 67 people in a remote area in Sudan, a medical group and survivors reported. The destruction occurred at the al-Zara gold mine, located in West Kordofan province – an area under the control of the paramilitary Rapid Support Forces, who have been at war with the country’s military for over three years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70695fe0-b1c3-11f1-b6db-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26173615409174.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70695fe0-b1c3-11f1-b6db-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26173615409174.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">773faf00-b1c2-11f1-a90f-af3f495acf71</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:54:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70695fe0-b1c3-11f1-b6db-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26173615409174.jpg">© Mohnd Bla, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ed Sheeran's tour in trouble after opening acts drop out in solidarity with rapper Macklemore</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-ed-sheeran-s-tour-in-trouble-after-opening-acts-drop-out-in-solidarity-with-rapper-macklemore</link><description>
Ed Sheeran’s tour of North and South America was plunged into chaos Tuesday when four of his supporting acts abruptly quit in solidarity with the rapper Macklemore, who was dropped for making pro-Palestinian comments onstage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9bc49cd6-b1b9-11f1-8d92-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-110700-110856-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9bc49cd6-b1b9-11f1-8d92-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-110700-110856-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a15796f8-b1b9-11f1-b275-392e33be7218</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:46:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Middle East: Iran war exposes limits of US power</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-middle-east-iran-war-exposes-limits-of-us-power</link><description>
Saudi Arabia’s crown prince sought backing Tuesday from the president of Egypt, his ally across the Red Sea, as the kingdom faces increased attacks by Yemen’s Houthi rebels on Saudi shipping and infrastructure that have helped drive a surge in global oil prices. France 24's Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6253094c-b1b9-11f1-9ff0-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-110323-110634-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6253094c-b1b9-11f1-9ff0-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-110323-110634-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">68237032-b1b9-11f1-ac98-cf844ad22bc2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:42:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ursula von der Leyen: EU chief pitches 'associate member' status for Canada</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-ursula-von-der-leyen-eu-chief-pitches-associate-member-status-for-canada</link><description>
EU chief Ursula von der Leyen raised the prospect Wednesday of Canada becoming the 27-nation bloc's first 'associate member', as she pitched closer cooperation on tech, defence and energy to Canadian leader Mark Carney.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53f187fe-b1b7-11f1-826d-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-110105-110216-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53f187fe-b1b7-11f1-826d-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-110105-110216-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a079af2-b1b7-11f1-ba3b-db2f5aa028f2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:41:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU – Canada: Standing ovation for Mark Carney</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-eu-%E2%80%93-canada-standing-ovation-for-mark-carney</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister was given a standing ovation at the European Parliament in Strasbourg, France on Wednesday as EU chief Ursula von der Leyen raised the prospect of Canada becoming the 27-nation bloc's first “associate member”. "We want to bring the relationship with Canada to the highest level possible," von der Leyen said as she pitched closer cooperation on tech, defence and energy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d32c6c58-b1b4-11f1-afcc-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/Carney-thumbnail.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d32c6c58-b1b4-11f1-afcc-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/Carney-thumbnail.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e871dc08-b1b2-11f1-b3b8-6b7ca022c6ce</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:22:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY - Ursula von der Leyen: Full State of the Union address</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-replay-ursula-von-der-leyen-full-state-of-the-union-address</link><description>
European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen proposed banning children under 13 from accessing social media, online games and chatbots during her annual State of the European Union speech in Strasbourg on Wednesday. She also proposed closer EU-Canada ties, including "associate member" status for Canada.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9077efa-b1b1-11f1-a71f-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-091212-103502-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9077efa-b1b1-11f1-a71f-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-091212-103502-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cfba58ee-b1b1-11f1-8dba-75caa5289289</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:07:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Trump set to sell 40,000 one-ton bombs to Israel</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260916-trump-set-to-sell-40-000-one-ton-bombs-to-israel</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, 16 September: The Washington Post reports that ICE is facing the fallout of their massive and 'reckless' hiring campaigns. Next, the Trump administration is planning to sell 2.8 billion dollars' worth of bombs to Israel. Also, Ed Sheeran's tour suffers another blow as his opening acts as well as his backing band drop out of his concerts. Finally, the French papers remember Catherine Ringer of the Rita Mitsuko band. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3841675c-b191-11f1-8845-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260916-0720-Live-CS0720.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3841675c-b191-11f1-8845-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260916-0720-Live-CS0720.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38be4f56-b187-11f1-a328-f92ff364e9af</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 09:33:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Emily BOYLE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Amnesty says Iran committed 'crimes against humanity' in 2022 protests crackdown</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-amnesty-international-says-iran-committed-crimes-against-humanity-in-2022-protests-crackdown</link><description>
