</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49c6f538-b1a9-11f1-af91-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/LA-chopper-crash-thumbnail.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49c6f538-b1a9-11f1-af91-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/LA-chopper-crash-thumbnail.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33ef337e-b1a9-11f1-8557-03ba46fc894d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 08:42:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russian drone attack on bus kills five in Ukraine's southeast</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-russian-drone-attack-on-bus-kills-five-in-ukraine-s-southeast</link><description>
Five people were killed and at least seven more were injured in a Russian drone attack on a passenger bus near the frontline in Ukraine's southeast on Wednesday, the regional governor said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32a17336-b19c-11f1-8958-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T064924Z-1003482524-RC24KNARF2CC-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32a17336-b19c-11f1-8958-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T064924Z-1003482524-RC24KNARF2CC-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29a8cc46-b19e-11f1-9784-83dc54a6a266</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 07:37:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32a17336-b19c-11f1-8958-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T064924Z-1003482524-RC24KNARF2CC-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Alina Smutko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Ed Sheeran's tour in trouble after Pro-Palestine acts drop out</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-ed-sheeran-s-tour-in-trouble-after-pro-palestine-acts-drop-out</link><description>
More artists scheduled to participate in Ed Sheeran’s tour of North and South America have quit in solidarity with the rapper Macklemore, who was dropped for making pro-Palestinian comments onstage. Among them are Irish acts Rowe and Lukas Graham, as well as Billie Eilish’s brother, Finneas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7781b4-b198-11f1-97c0-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26257691242503.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7781b4-b198-11f1-97c0-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26257691242503.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6138d66-b198-11f1-8ca8-9164e56b78fd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 06:54:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7781b4-b198-11f1-97c0-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26257691242503.jpg">© Andy Kropa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French ex-culture minister Rachida Dati goes on trial in Carlos Ghosn graft case</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/france/20260916-french-ex-culture-minister-rachida-dati-goes-on-trial-in-carlos-ghosn-graft-case</link><description>
France's former culture minister Rachida Dati goes on trial at a Paris court Wednesday in a corruption case involving charges of lobbying for Renault-Nissan when she was a European parliament member. The high-profile case centres on a contract signed in October 2009 between Dati and fugitive businessman Carlos Ghosn, then head of Renault-Nissan. Dati denies the allegations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dbc05898-b191-11f1-ac5c-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C82E79E.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dbc05898-b191-11f1-ac5c-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C82E79E.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb610be8-b195-11f1-9d44-b1f7d2c4434c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 06:51:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dbc05898-b191-11f1-ac5c-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C82E79E.jpg">© Julien de Rosa, Joseph Eid, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Hong Kong unveils first five-year plan to cement position as global financial hub</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260916-hong-kong-unveils-first-five-year-plan-to-cement-position-as-global-financial-hub</link><description>
Hong ⁠Kong leader ​John Lee on Wednesday unveiled the city's first five-year plan to boost its global position as a financial hub. The plan serves as a social and economic roadmap detailing the city-state's strategic priorities, including an aim to expand technology ties with mainland China.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4b2df04-b18f-11f1-b11e-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259169257573.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4b2df04-b18f-11f1-b11e-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259169257573.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">579e5e40-b18f-11f1-8ef2-9d69488b4342</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 05:54:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4b2df04-b18f-11f1-b11e-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259169257573.jpg">© Chan Long Heic, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Kylian Mbappé and Real Madrid defeat Elche despite late scare</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260916-football-kylian-mbapp%C3%A9-and-real-madrid-defeat-elche-despite-late-scare</link><description>
Real Madrid narrowly defeated Elche (3-2) in Matchday 6 of La Liga. Kylian Mbappé scored a goal and provided an assist.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50523698-b171-11f1-9220-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-real-1-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50523698-b171-11f1-9220-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-real-1-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a9c6036c-b171-11f1-9814-3f3753549424</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 05:28:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU chief calls for creation of ‘European Security Council’, backs partnership with Canada</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-live-eu-chief-ursula-von-der-leyen-gives-state-of-the-union-address</link><description>
EU chief Ursula von der Leyen called for the creation of a "European Security Council", with countries including Britain and Ukraine, in her State of the European Union speech to the European Parliament in Strasbourg on Wednesday. Addressing this year's special guest, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney, von der Leyen said she wants to open the door for Canada to become the bloc's first associate member.
